{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization proving 29 * tau(G) <= 81 * nu(G) (tau(G) <= (81 / 29) * nu(G) ~= 2.793103 * nu(G)) for every finite simple graph G, where nu(G) is the triangle packing number and tau(G) is the triangle transversal number, strictly improving Sichen Wang's 165/59 bound (arXiv:2609.13831). Extends Wang's MIT-licensed sichen-wang/tuza-lean library with helper-arborescence coupling, unmerged colored-family covers, and opposite-edge elimination, together with non-vacuity checks nu(K_4) = 1 and tau(K_4) = 2.",
  "authors": [
